<a name="taming"></a>
### 1️⃣ Taming Transformers for High‑Resolution Image Synthesis  
*Paper*: `taming_transformers_for_high-resolution_image_synthesis.tex`  
*Repo*: `CompVis/taming-transformers` → `/workplace/taming-transformers`

#### Core Mathematical Components

| # | Symbol / Term | LaTeX (as in the paper) | Explanation |
|---|---------------|--------------------------|-------------|
| 1 | Encoder output (continuous latent) | `\mathbf{z}_e(\mathbf{x}) = \operatorname{Encoder}(\mathbf{x})\in\mathbb{R}^{H\times W\times D}` | Convolution‑Transformer encoder producing a spatial grid of D‑dim vectors. |
| 2 | Quantization (nearest‑code‑book entry) | `\mathbf{z}_q(\mathbf{x}) = \operatorname{Quantize}\big(\mathbf{z}_e(\mathbf{x})\big) = \mathbf{e}_{k^\*},\quad k^\*=\arg\min_k\|\mathbf{z}_e(\mathbf{x})-\mathbf{e}_k\|_2` | Selects the closest code‑book vector **eₖ**. |
| 3 | Commitment loss | `\mathcal{L}_\text{commit}= \big\|\operatorname{sg}\big[\mathbf{z}_e(\mathbf{x})\big]-\mathbf{z}_q(\mathbf{x})\big\|_2^2` | Encourages encoder output to stay near the chosen codebook entry. |
| 4 | Code‑book loss | `\mathcal{L}_\text{codebook}= \big\|\mathbf{z}_e(\mathbf{x})-\operatorname{sg}\big[\mathbf{z}_q(\mathbf{x})\big]\big\|_2^2` | Updates codebook vectors toward encoder output. |
| 5 | Reconstruction loss | `\mathcal{L}_\text{rec}= \|\mathbf{x}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}\|_2^2` | Pixel‑wise MSE between input and decoded image. |
| 6 | Perceptual loss (VGG) | `\mathcal{L}_\text{perc}= \sum_{l}\frac{1}{N_l}\big\|\phi_l(\mathbf{x})-\phi_l(\hat{\mathbf{x}})\big\|_2^2` | Uses VGG‑19 features **φₗ**. |
| 7 | Adversarial GAN loss (PatchGAN) | `\mathcal{L}_\text{GAN}= \mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}}[\log D(\mathbf{x})] + \mathbb{E}_{\hat{\mathbf{x}}}[\log(1-D(\hat{\mathbf{x}}))]` |
| 8 | Full objective | `\mathcal{L}= \lambda_\text{rec}\mathcal{L}_\text{rec} + \lambda_\text{perc}\mathcal{L}_\text{perc} + \lambda_\text{commit}\mathcal{L}_\text{commit} + \lambda_\text{code}\mathcal{L}_\text{codebook} + \lambda_\text{GAN}\mathcal{L}_\text{GAN}` |

#### Where the Equations Live in the Code

| Eq. # | Repo‑relative file | Class / Function | Key implementation details |
|-------|--------------------|------------------|----------------------------|
| 1‑2 | `modules/vqvae/quantize.py` | `VectorQuantizer.forward` | Nearest‑neighbor lookup (`torch.cdist`). |
| 3 | same file | `VectorQuantizer.loss` | `commitment_loss = ((z_e.detach() - z_q)**2).mean()` |
| 4 | same file | `VectorQuantizer.loss` | `codebook_loss = ((z_e - z_q.detach())**2).mean()` |
| 5 | `models/autoencoder.py` | `AutoEncoder.forward` | `recon_loss = F.mse_loss(x_recon, x)` |
| 6 | `modules/perceptual.py` | `PerceptualLoss` | Uses a pre‑trained VGG‑19, extracts selected layers, computes MSE. |
| 7 | `models/discriminator.py` + `train.py` | `Discriminator` + `torch.nn.BCEWithLogitsLoss` | Standard binary‑cross‑entropy on real/fake logits. |
| 8 | `train.py` | `train_one_epoch` (loss aggregation) | Combines the five terms with the λ‑coefficients defined in the config file. |

